### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS Lex bot using the `aws_lex_bot` resource. The bot is configured with basic settings such as `child_directed`, `name`, and `locale`. Additionally, it includes nested blocks for `abort_statement` and `clarification_prompt` to handle user interactions.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_lex_bot" "my_lex_bot" {
  name                = "MyLexBot"
  child_directed      = false
  locale              = "en-US"
  idle_session_ttl_in_seconds = 300
  process_behavior    = "BUILD"

  abort_statement {
    message {
      content     = "Sorry, I didn't understand that."
      content_type = "PlainText"
    }
  }

  clarification_prompt {
    max_attempts = 2
    message {
      content     = "Can you please provide more information?"
      content_type = "PlainText"
    }
  }

  intent {
    intent_name   = "GreetingIntent"
    intent_version = "$LATEST"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up a basic AWS Lex bot with the specified attributes and nested blocks. The bot is configured to handle user interactions with an abort statement and a clarification prompt. The intent block specifies the intent that the bot will use.

