### Description

This Terraform program creates an S3 bucket and a Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream configured with an extended S3 destination. The Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream will deliver data to the specified S3 bucket. The program ensures that the S3 bucket is created before the Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream to avoid any dependency issues.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "firehose_destination_bucket" {
  bucket = "firehose-destination-bucket-${var.environment}"
  acl    = "private"
  tags = {
    Name        = "FirehoseDestinationBucket"
    Environment = var.environment
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "firehose_role" {
  name = "firehose-role-${var.environment}"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "firehose_policy" {
  name = "firehose-policy-${var.environment}"
  role = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "s3:AbortMultipartUpload",
          "s3:GetBucketLocation",
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:ListBucket",
          "s3:ListBucketMultipartUploads",
          "s3:PutObject"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = [
          aws_s3_bucket.firehose_destination_bucket.arn,
          "${aws_s3_bucket.firehose_destination_bucket.arn}/*"
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "firehose_delivery_stream" {
  name        = "firehose-delivery-stream-${var.environment}"
  destination = "extended_s3"

  extended_s3_configuration {
    role_arn           = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.arn
    bucket_arn         = aws_s3_bucket.firehose_destination_bucket.arn
    buffering_interval = 300
    buffering_size     = 5
    compression_format = "UNCOMPRESSED"
    prefix             = "firehose/"
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "FirehoseDeliveryStream"
    Environment = var.environment
  }
}

variable "environment" {
  description = "Environment tag for resources"
  default     = "dev"
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket named `firehose-destination-bucket-${var.environment}` is created. The bucket is private and tagged with the environment.
3. **IAM Role and Policy**: An IAM role named `firehose-role-${var.environment}` is created with a trust policy allowing Firehose to assume the role. An IAM policy is attached to this role granting necessary S3 permissions.
4. **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: A Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream named `firehose-delivery-stream-${var.environment}` is created with an extended S3 destination. The stream is configured to buffer data for 300 seconds or 5 MB before delivering it to the S3 bucket. The stream is tagged with the environment.
5. **Variable**: A variable `environment` is defined with a default value of `dev` to allow tagging resources with the environment they belong to.

