The Terraform configuration provided has some issues with the placement of the `url_exclusion_patterns` and `url_inclusion_patterns` arguments. According to the Terraform AWS provider schema, these arguments should be placed within the `web_crawler_configuration` block under the `urls` block.

Here is the corrected Terraform HCL program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source" {
  index_id = "your-kendra-index-id"
  name     = "MyKendraDataSource"
  type     = "WEBCRAWLER"

  configuration {
    web_crawler_configuration {
      urls {
        seed_url_configuration {
          seed_urls = ["https://example.com"]
        }

        url_exclusion_patterns = [
          "https://example.com/exclude/*",
          "https://example.com/private/*"
        ]

        url_inclusion_patterns = [
          "https://example.com/include/*",
          "https://example.com/public/*"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This configuration ensures that the `url_exclusion_patterns` and `url_inclusion_patterns` are correctly placed within the `web_crawler_configuration` block under the `urls` block, which should resolve the validation errors.

