### Description
This Terraform program creates a basic Amazon Kendra index with user group resolution configuration. It includes an IAM role required by the Kendra index to operate. The IAM role has an assume role policy that allows Kendra permissions.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "kendra_index_role" {
  name = "kendra-index-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kendra.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kendra_index" "basic_kendra_index" {
  name     = "basic-kendra-index"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.kendra_index_role.arn

  user_group_resolution_configuration {
    user_group_resolution_mode = "AWS_SSO"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to any other region as needed.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `kendra-index-role` is created. The assume role policy allows the Kendra service to assume this role.
3. **Kendra Index**: A Kendra index named `basic-kendra-index` is created. It uses the IAM role created earlier. The `user_group_resolution_configuration` block specifies the mode as `AWS_SSO`, which enables user group resolution using AWS Single Sign-On.

