### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_s3_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-unique-s3-bucket-name"  # Replace with a unique bucket name
  acl    = "private"  # Set the ACL as needed
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" "my_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_s3_bucket.id  # Reference the bucket ID

  rule {
    object_ownership = "BucketOwnerPreferred"  # Set object ownership to BucketOwnerPreferred
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to any other valid AWS region as needed.
2. **S3 Bucket Resource**: An S3 bucket is created with a specified name (`my-unique-s3-bucket-name`). Ensure the bucket name is globally unique across all existing bucket names in Amazon S3. The `acl` is set to `private` by default, but you can adjust this based on your requirements.
3. **Ownership Controls Resource**: The `aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls` resource is configured to reference the `id` of the previously created S3 bucket. Inside the `rule` block, the `object_ownership` is set to `BucketOwnerPreferred`, which ensures that the bucket owner has full control over the objects stored in the bucket.

