### Description
This Terraform program creates a custom DAX subnet group by first setting up a VPC and a subnet within that VPC. The DAX subnet group is then created using the subnet ID of the previously created subnet.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "custom_vpc" {
  cidr_block           = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_support   = true
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
}

resource "aws_subnet" "custom_subnet" {
  vpc_id                  = aws_vpc.custom_vpc.id
  cidr_block              = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone       = "us-west-2a"
  map_public_ip_on_launch = true
}

resource "aws_dax_subnet_group" "custom_dax_subnet_group" {
  name       = "custom-dax-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.custom_subnet.id]
}
```

This configuration sets up a VPC with a specific CIDR block, creates a subnet within that VPC, and then creates a DAX subnet group using the subnet ID of the created subnet. All resources are fully specified and meet the requirements outlined in the prompt and the typed provider contract.

