### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS SageMaker Pipeline resource. The pipeline requires a display name and a name, which are provided as input variables with default values. Additionally, the program includes nested blocks for parallelism configuration and pipeline definition S3 location, both of which are required by the schema.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "pipeline_display_name" {
  description = "The display name of the SageMaker pipeline"
  default     = "MySageMakerPipeline"
}

variable "pipeline_name" {
  description = "The name of the SageMaker pipeline"
  default     = "my-sagemaker-pipeline"
}

variable "s3_bucket" {
  description = "The S3 bucket where the pipeline definition is stored"
  default     = "my-sagemaker-pipeline-bucket"
}

variable "s3_object_key" {
  description = "The S3 object key where the pipeline definition is stored"
  default     = "pipeline-definition.json"
}

variable "max_parallel_execution_steps" {
  description = "The maximum number of parallel execution steps"
  default     = 10
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_pipeline" "sagemaker_pipeline" {
  pipeline_display_name = var.pipeline_display_name
  pipeline_name         = var.pipeline_name

  parallelism_configuration {
    max_parallel_execution_steps = var.max_parallel_execution_steps
  }

  pipeline_definition_s3_location {
    bucket     = var.s3_bucket
    object_key = var.s3_object_key
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up an AWS SageMaker Pipeline with the specified display name, name, and configuration details. The pipeline definition is assumed to be stored in an S3 bucket, and the maximum number of parallel execution steps is configurable.

