To address the authentication failure error, we need to ensure that the AWS provider is configured with valid credentials. This typically involves setting up the AWS CLI or configuring environment variables with your AWS access key and secret key.

Below is the corrected Terraform configuration with a placeholder for AWS credentials. You should replace `<YOUR_ACCESS_KEY>` and `<YOUR_SECRET_KEY>` with your actual AWS credentials.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region     = "us-west-2"
  access_key = "<YOUR_ACCESS_KEY>"
  secret_key = "<YOUR_SECRET_KEY>"
}

data "aws_ami" "amazon_linux_2" {
  most_recent = true
  owners     = ["amazon"]

  filter {
    name   = "name"
    values = ["amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2"]
  }
}

resource "aws_instance" "example_instance" {
