### Description
The Terraform program defines an AWS infrastructure that provisions an EC2 instance and sets up a daily backup plan using AWS Backup. The program includes the creation of an EC2 key pair for SSH access, an EC2 instance, an AWS Backup vault, and a Backup plan. The Backup plan is configured to run daily at midnight.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# Generate an AWS Key Pair for SSH access
resource "aws_key_pair" "ec2_key_pair" {
  key_name   = "my-ec2-key-pair"
  public_key = file("${path.module}/id_rsa.pub")  # Path to your public key file
}

# Create an EC2 instance
resource "aws_instance" "ec2_instance" {
  ami           = "ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0"  # Ensure this AMI is available in your region
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
  key_name      = aws_key_pair.ec2_key_pair.key_name
  security_groups = ["default"]  # Replace with appropriate security group if needed
}

# Create an AWS Backup Vault
resource "aws_backup_vault" "backup_vault" {
  name = "my-backup-vault"
}

# Create an AWS Backup Plan
resource "aws_backup_plan" "backup_plan" {
  name = "daily_backup_plan"

  rule {
    rule_name         = "DailyBackupRule"
    target_vault_name = aws_backup_vault.backup_vault.name
    schedule          = "cron(0 0 * * ? *)"  # Daily at midnight
  }
}
```

### Notes
1. **Key Pair Public Key Path**: The path to the public key file has been changed to `${path.module}/id_rsa.pub` to ensure the file is part of the configuration source code. Make sure to place your public key file (`id_rsa.pub`) in the same directory as your Terraform configuration files.
2. **Security Group**: The security group is set to "default". Replace it with an appropriate security group if needed.
3. **AMI ID**: Ensure the AMI ID (`ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0`) is available in your specified region (`us-west-2`). You may need to update this ID based on your requirements.

