### Description
The Terraform program defines an internal-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB) within an AWS VPC. The ALB is associated with a private subnet, ensuring that it only serves traffic within the VPC and does not have a public IP address. The configuration includes a VPC, a private subnet, and the ALB itself. The ALB is named to comply with AWS naming conventions, avoiding the prefix "internal-".

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

resource "aws_subnet" "internal_subnet" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"
  map_public_ip_on_launch = false
}

resource "aws_lb" "internal_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-internal-load-balancer"
  internal           = true
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  subnets            = [aws_subnet.internal_subnet.id]
}
```

This configuration ensures that the load balancer is correctly set up as an internal-facing ALB within the specified VPC and subnet. The name of the load balancer has been changed to "my-internal-load-balancer" to avoid the naming restriction mentioned in the error message.

