### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and a target group to forward traffic to one or more EC2 instances. The ALB is configured to listen on HTTP port 80 and forward traffic to the target group. The target group is set up to handle HTTP traffic on port 80.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "my_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"

  subnet_mapping {
    subnet_id = "subnet-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with your subnet ID
  }

  security_groups = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]  # Replace with your security group ID

  access_logs {
    bucket = "my-alb-logs-bucket"  # Replace with your S3 bucket name
    prefix = "alb-logs/"
  }

  enable_deletion_protection = false
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "my_target_group" {
  name     = "my-target-group"
  port     = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id   = "vpc-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with your VPC ID

  health_check {
    path                = "/"
    interval            = 30
    timeout             = 5
    healthy_threshold   = 5
    unhealthy_threshold = 2
  }

  target_type = "instance"
}
```

### Notes
- Replace `"subnet-0123456789abcdef0"`, `"sg-0123456789abcdef0"`, `"my-alb-logs-bucket"`, and `"vpc-0123456789abcdef0"` with your actual AWS resource IDs and names.
- Ensure that the security group allows inbound traffic on port 80 from the ALB.
- The `enable_deletion_protection` is set to `false` for easier deletion during testing. Set it to `true` in production environments to prevent accidental deletion.

