  default_network_acl_id = aws_vpc.my_vpc.default_network_acl_id

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    rule_no     = 100
    action      = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
  }

  ingress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    rule_no     = 100
    action      = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
  }
}
```

This configuration creates a VPC with a specified CIDR block and enables DNS support and hostnames. It then creates a default network ACL associated with this VPC, allowing all traffic (both ingress and egress) from and to any source.

